{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi… I’ve been feeling really sick. I was having trouble breathing and felt super weak. My blood sugar was really high when I checked it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. The ER team told me your blood sugar was 824 and you weren’t making insulin. You’ve had DKA before, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… I know. I haven’t been taking my insulin. I missed a few days. I was sick with a cold and just didn’t feel like doing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But stopping insulin, even when you're sick, can be dangerous. Your body starts breaking down fat, which makes acids build up—called ketoacidosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, I just… didn’t think it would get this bad. I didn’t mean to hurt myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t think you did. But the team wanted to make sure you’re safe, so psychiatry will check in with you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I’m not suicidal. I just get overwhelmed sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. Right now, we’re treating your DKA with an insulin drip and fluids. Your potassium was high when you came in—7.1—but it’s coming down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "High potassium? I thought diabetics usually have low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good question. Usually yes, but in DKA, acidosis can push potassium out of cells, making it high at first. We gave you calcium gluconate to protect your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… that makes sense. My kidneys were off too, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your creatinine was 1.7, which means your kidneys were stressed from dehydration. But with fluids, it’s already down to 1.1. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been so dry. My mouth feels like sand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s from being dehydrated. We’re giving you IV fluids to fix that. You’ll feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. What about the breathing? I was breathing so fast."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s called Kussmaul breathing. Your body was trying to blow off acid to balance your blood. It’s improving now that we’re treating the DKA."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… I didn’t know that had a name."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also put in a central line in your neck for better access. It helps us give meds and fluids safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It feels weird, but I don’t mind. Is it safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and a chest X-ray confirmed it’s in the right place. Your lungs look clear—no pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had a cough, but everyone at home is sick with a cold."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely a viral URI. We gave you antibiotics just in case, but your urine test didn’t show infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been in outpatient treatment for alcohol. I haven’t had a drink in over two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2161-09-12 19:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’re giving you thiamine and multivitamins to support that. Your CIWA score is low, so no withdrawal signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2161-09-13 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are improving. Your blood sugar is down to 180, and your acid levels are normalizing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2161-09-13 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can I eat something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2161-09-13 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re starting you on a regular diet. We’ll switch from the insulin drip to your regular shots—Lantus in the morning and at bedtime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2161-09-13 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the sliding scale?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2161-09-13 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep that. The endocrine team reviewed your case and said to keep your Lantus dose the same but adjust the sliding scale if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2161-09-13 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll try not to miss doses again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2161-09-13 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. You’ve also been seen by psychiatry. They recommend continuing your venlafaxine and mirtazapine and following up with your therapist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2161-09-13 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve been feeling better mentally, but stress still gets to me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2161-09-13 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. Managing diabetes is hard, especially with other challenges. We’ll make sure you have support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2161-09-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. Your labs this morning are almost all normal. Blood sugar 173, potassium 3.5, creatinine 0.7."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2161-09-14 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! Can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2161-09-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you today. One thing—your blood cultures showed a little bacteria, but it’s likely just skin contamination, not a real infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2161-09-14 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. Should I worry?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2161-09-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, not at all. We’ll follow up if anything changes, but it’s very likely nothing. Just keep taking care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2161-09-14 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’ll follow up with my doctors and take my insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2161-09-14 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if your blood sugar goes above 300 or you feel sick again. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2161-09-12 19:02:00",
    "admission_end": "2161-09-14 15:35:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with type 1 diabetes, depression, and a history of alcohol use disorder, was admitted for diabetic ketoacidosis after missing several days of insulin, likely triggered by a viral upper respiratory infection. She presented with severe hyperglycemia (glucose 824), metabolic acidosis, hyperkalemia (K+ 7.1), and acute kidney injury (Cr 1.7), with signs of dehydration and Kussmaul respirations. She was treated in the ICU with IV fluids, insulin drip, and electrolyte management, including calcium gluconate for hyperkalemia. Her condition improved rapidly, with resolution of DKA and normalization of renal function. An insulin drip was transitioned to her home regimen of glargine and sliding scale insulin. Psychiatry evaluated her for passive suicidal ideation related to insulin noncompliance but found no contraindication to discharge. She was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up plans for endocrinology, mental health, and primary care, and pending blood culture results were deemed likely contaminants.",
    "problems": [
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with ketoacidosis without coma",
      "Suicidal ideations",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Hyperkalemia",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with diabetic neuropathy, unspecified",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with unspecified diabetic retinopathy without macular edema",
      "Alcohol dependence, uncomplicated",
      "Hypovolemia",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Atherosclerotic heart disease of native coronary artery without angina pectoris",
      "Patient's other noncompliance with medication regimen",
      "Encounter for immunization"
    ]
  }
}
